WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
BUKOLA AYODELE:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.340
about Cloud Function, security,
and where to store things.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.440
I'm Bukola, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.560
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.690
Cloud Functions is a
lightweight platform

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.670
for creating standalone
functions, which

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.120
is a great way to create
pieces of a larger workflow.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.880
With the newly launched ability
to specify the minimum number

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.420
of instances, you no longer
need to worry about cold starts

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.070
delaying your workflows.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.440
Try it out for yourself
with the linked tutorial.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.970
Speaking of Cloud
Functions, did you

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.220
know it now has
native integration

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.020
with Secret Manager?

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.750
Secret Manager is a fully
managed storage system

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.440
for keeping secrets like
API keys or passwords.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.060
These two great services
are even better together.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.620
So check out how you can get
better at keeping a secret.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.150
The sooner you think
about security,

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.180
the less downstream issues
you're likely to have.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.870
That is why it can help to have
an on-demand scanning setup

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.570
as part of your CI/CD process.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.240
You can read more about
how on-demand scanning can

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.640
help detect vulnerabilities
in containers

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.880
and follow along in
tutorials to stay secure.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.150
While you may not be able to
move all those boxes in garage

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.180
to Cloud Storage, it's a perfect
solution for object storage

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.520
no matter what your
application needs.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.940
If you're not sure which storage
class or location to use,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.740
don't worry, Priyanka
breaks it down

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.095
in this quick sketchnote
and blog post.

00:01:22.095 --> 00:01:23.970
If you want to read
about these announcements

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.410
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.890
Any thoughts or idea, leave
a comment or tweet us,

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.280
and we'll see you in the Cloud.

